{{Codex|The versatile Cinta can fire arrows in quick succession, quickly charge a shock wave, or fully charge a powerful focused shot.}}
'''Cinta''' is a [[Duviri]] bow wielded by the [[Dax Arcus]]. It is capable of firing "perfect" shots when releasing the trigger just before a full charge, resulting in a large projectile for dealing with groups of enemies.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*In addition to uncharged shots, this weapon can fire one of two types of charged shots, depending on where the charge meter is released.
**Releasing the shot within '''70%''' to '''90%''' of a full charge, indicated by white brackets and the reticle turning yellow, will perform a "Perfect Shot", firing an energy shockwave dealing pure {{D|Heat}} damage, guaranteed {{D|Knockdown}}, and a significantly larger projectile with [[Infinite Body Punch Through]].
**Releasing the shot when the meter is fully charged will perform a "Charged Shot", firing a single arrow dealing heavy {{D|Puncture}} damage, with higher [[critical chance]] and [[critical multiplier]] than that of Perfect Shots.

{{Advantages|class=Bow|}}
{{Disadvantages|class=Bow|}}
{{Acquisition|Cinta's main and component blueprints are acquired by solving [[Duviri Enigma|Enigma]] puzzles in [[The Duviri Experience|Duviri]], having a 30% chance to drop one part from any puzzle completion. All blueprints are [[Trading|tradable]].}}
{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*There is a gap between the Perfect Shot window and full charge where releasing the charge will fire uncharged shots instead.
*Although similar to {{Weapon|Nataruk}}, Cinta can make use of {{M|Split Flights}}, whereas the former cannot.

==Known Bugs==
*{{M|Galvanized Aptitude}} is multiplicative to base damage sources on uncharged, perfect and charged shots.

==Trivia==
*''Cinta'' is the [https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cinta#Indonesian Malay/Indonesian] word for "love", and [https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cinta#Spanish Spanish] for "tape" or "ribbon".
*Prior to {{ver|33.5}}, the Cinta had an [[Alternate Fire]] that could prime landmines while having the player leap backward. This feature was only intended for the [[Dax Arcus]] enemy, and was removed from the player version due to animation oddities and low damage.

